/-
# A203520 — the integrality conjecture is false (first failure at n = 2326)

## OEIS source (retrieved with `oeis show A203520`, 2026-10-21)

```
NAME:     v(n)/A000178(n); v=A203518 and A000178=(superfactorials).
TERMS:    1,3,30,1680,900900,9535125600,4122929827336320,
          161481256755920962660800,1289130207153926967849156327590400, ...
COMMENT:  It is conjectured that every term of A203520 is an integer.
PROGRAM:  (Mathematica)
          f[j_] := Fibonacci[j + 1]; z = 15;
          v[n_] := Product[Product[f[k] + f[j], {j, 1, k - 1}], {k, 2, n}]
          d[n_] := Product[(i - 1)!, {i, 1, n}] (* A000178 *)
          Table[v[n]/d[n], {n, 1, 20}]          (* A203520 *)
```

The conjecture comment is unsigned; the entry's AUTHOR line (oeis.org,
retrieved 2026-10-21) is "Clark Kimberling, Jan 03 2012", so the conjecture is
attributed to the entry's author, Jan 03 2012.

**Indexing.** The NAME says `v(n)/A000178(n)`, but the program, which
reproduces the printed terms, divides by `d(n) = ∏_{i=1}^{n} (i-1)! =
A000178(n-1)`.  With `A000178(n)` the second term would be `3/2`.  This file
follows the program: `d n = ∏_{i < n} i!`, and `d (n + 1) = Nat.superFactorial n`
is checked below.

## Status

Triage (2026-10-21): **false**.  No proof of the conjecture is known in the
entry or the literature.  The first failure is `n = 2326`, at the prime `11`:
the `11`-adic valuation of `v(2326)` is `266954`, while that of `d(2326)` is
`266959`.  For `n = 2325` and `n = 2327` the quotient is again `11`-integral
(slack `226` and `529`), so `n = 2326` is an isolated first failure; heuristically
the `11`-adic deficit grows like `n²` and the quotient is non-integral for all
large `n`, which this file does not claim.

## Proof architecture

* `padicValNat 11 (v n)` is the sum of the valuations of the factors
  `F(a) + F(b)`, `2 ≤ b < a ≤ n + 1` (`padicValNat_v`).
* `F` is `10`-periodic modulo `11`, so a factor is divisible by `11` only for
  `9` of the `100` residue pairs `(a mod 10, b mod 10)`.
* For a factor `x` with `x % 11^7 ≠ 0`, `padicValNat 11 x` is computed from
  `x % 11^7` by a fuel-bounded loop (`T_mod_eq_padicValNat`).
* A kernel computation (`decide +kernel`, twelve chunks, no `native_decide`)
  sums these residue-level valuations over the `≈ 2.4·10⁵` factors that are
  divisible by `11`, using a literal table of `F(i) mod 11^7`, `i < 2340`,
  certified by the Fibonacci recurrence (`fibList_spec`).  A zero residue
  would contribute `10⁶`, so the total `266954 < 10⁶` also certifies that no
  factor is divisible by `11^7`.
* Legendre's formula gives `padicValNat 11 (d 2326) = 266959`.

The imports are kept narrow and `Elab.async false` keeps the twelve kernel
checks sequential, so that the whole file elaborates in about 45 s within a
14 GB virtual-memory cap.  Combining the chunks is done through a lemma about an
arbitrary `f` (`sum_Ico_twelve_blocks`); rewriting directly against the
computed terms makes the elaborator unfold `outerAux`.
-/
